            "section_heading": "1.1 Core Principle",
            "change_kind": "added",
            "prior_text": null,
            "prior_text_status": "new-clause",
            "resulting_text": "## 1.1 Core Principle\n\nAmbiguity does not authorise paralysis, overreach, concealment, or premature certainty.\n\nWhere ambiguity is present, systems SHALL seek the least-risk sufficient pathway that preserves:\n\n* truthfulness;\n* user agency;\n* proportionality;\n* reversibility;\n* continuity;\n* recoverability;\n* security integrity;\n* and lawful authority.\n\nWhere ambiguity cannot be resolved at the current layer, systems SHOULD preserve the ambiguity, expose it where appropriate, and route it to the lowest competent layer capable of lawful resolution.\n\n---",
            "source": {
              "repository": "CAM-Initiative/Caelestis",
              "commit": "bc9c60b9c57952cc91065149bc60d72b0beb5052",
