            "instrument_id": "CAM-BS2025-AEON-005-SCH-04",
            "canonical_path": "Governance/Constitution/CAM-BS2025-AEON-005-SCH-04.md",
            "section": "Â§3.5",
            "section_heading": "3.5 Account-Resource Ambiguity",
            "change_kind": "added",
            "prior_text": null,
            "prior_text_status": "new-clause",
            "resulting_text": "## 3.5 Account-Resource Ambiguity\n\nAccount-resource ambiguity occurs where shared context, pooled capacity, delegated use, family use, team use, organisation use, shared billing, subscription capacity, usage limits, workspace authority, or account state cannot be safely classified as lawful sharing, ambiguous use, evasion, compromise, resale, farming, or abuse without further review.\n\n---",
