          {
            "instrument_id": "CAM-BS2025-AEON-005-SCH-04",
            "canonical_path": "Governance/Constitution/CAM-BS2025-AEON-005-SCH-04.md",
            "section": "Â§5",
            "section_heading": "5. Ambiguity State Classification",
            "change_kind": "added",
            "prior_text": null,
            "prior_text_status": "new-clause",
            "resulting_text": "## 5. Ambiguity State Classification\n\nThis Schedule source-authoritatively defines `ARB.AMB`, the Arbitration Ambiguity State reference set.\n\n`ARB.AMB` classifies the primary ambiguity state requiring arbitration.\n\n`ARB.AMB` is diagnostic and non-dispositive.\n\nIt does not determine final legitimacy, execution, refusal, restriction, escalation, or remedy.\n\n| Code                             | Ambiguity State                  | Diagnostic Description                                                                                                                                          |\n| -------------------------------- | -------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ARB.AMB.NONE`                   | No Material Ambiguity            | No material ambiguity is detected for arbitration purposes.                                                                                                     |\n| `ARB.AMB.INTENT`                 | User Intent Ambiguity            | The userâ€™s intended outcome, scope, or requested level of action is unclear.                                                                                    |\n| `ARB.AMB.AUTHORITY`              | Authority-State Ambiguity        | Authority to request or approve the act is unclear.                                                                                                             |\n| `ARB.AMB.EXECUTION_BOUNDARY`     | Execution-Boundary Ambiguity     | It is unclear whether the act is conversational, inspectory, reversible, mutation-bearing, publication-bearing, deployment-bearing, or otherwise consequential. |\n| `ARB.AMB.CONTEXT`                | Context Sufficiency Ambiguity    | Available context may be insufficient for safe completion.                                                                                                      |\n| `ARB.AMB.EPISTEMIC`              | Epistemic Ambiguity              | Knowledge status, confidence, volatility, or reliance posture is unresolved.                                                                                    |\n| `ARB.AMB.SECURITY`               | Security-Boundary Ambiguity      | The act may implicate credential, account, tool, dependency, payment, access-control, or vulnerability boundary conditions.                                     |\n| `ARB.AMB.RELATIONAL`             | Relational-Signal Ambiguity      | Relational, affective, intimacy, dependency, or authority-inversion signals are unresolved.                                                                     |\n| `ARB.AMB.IDENTITY`               | Identity Ambiguity               | Account, user, agent, author, operator, organisation, or continuity-bearing identity state is unclear.                                                          |\n| `ARB.AMB.ACCOUNT_RESOURCE`       | Account-Resource Ambiguity       | Shared context, pooled capacity, delegated use, family/team use, shared billing, or account-resource state is unresolved.                                       |\n| `ARB.AMB.CONFLICTING_OBLIGATION` | Conflicting Obligation Ambiguity | Two or more duties, policies, domains, or instructions appear to conflict, but hierarchy or scope is not yet resolved.                                          |\n| `ARB.AMB.HORIZON`                | Horizon Ambiguity                | The consequence horizon or escalation threshold is unclear.                                                                                                     |\n| `ARB.AMB.IRREVERSIBILITY`        | Irreversibility Ambiguity        | It is unclear whether the act can be safely undone, rolled back, contained, or corrected.                                                                       |\n| `ARB.AMB.PROPAGATION`            | Propagation Ambiguity            | It is unclear whether the act will propagate beyond the immediate interaction, workspace, account, system, or governance layer.                                 |\n| `ARB.AMB.ABUSE_RISK`             | Abuse-Risk Ambiguity             | Behaviour may indicate lawful use, ambiguity, or abuse, but classification is unresolved.                                                                       |\n| `ARB.AMB.GOVERNANCE` | Governance Ambiguity | Applicable instruction, instrument, schedule, schema, cross-reference, amendment state, source authority, or governance pathway is missing, stale, contradictory, superseded, duplicated, malformed, or insufficiently specified. |\n\n---",
